& -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$G=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 4 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n| $4F-\\frac{1}{2}G=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |" 13194139535481 17592186045443 true] [17592186299869 1074 "We multiply each entry of $F$ by $4$ and each entry of $G$ by $\\frac{1}{2},$ and then subtract the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4F-\\frac{1}{2}G & =4[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 & -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot 4 & 4\\cdot (-1) & 4\\cdot 0 & 4\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-6)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16 & -4 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16-1 & -4-0 & 0-2 & 8-(-3)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}15 & -4 & -2 & 11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535481 17592186045443 false] [17592186299869 1074 "We multiply each entry of $F$ by $4$ and each entry of $G$ by $\\frac{1}{2},$ and then subtract the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4F-\\frac{1}{2}G & =4\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 4 & -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4\\cdot 4 & 4\\cdot (-1) & 4\\cdot 0 & 4\\cdot 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-6)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}16 & -4 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}16-1 & -4-0 & 0-2 & 8-(-3)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}15 & -4 & -2 & 11\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535481 17592186045443 true] [17592186299873 1071 "Calculate $\\frac{2}{3}M+2N$, where\n$M=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 15 \\\\ -12 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$N=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & \\frac{1}{2} & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n| $\\frac{2}{3}M+2N=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $-2$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-12$ | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" 13194139535481 17592186045443 false] [17592186299873 1071 "Calculate $\\frac{2}{3}M+2N$, where\n$M=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 15 \\\\ -12 & 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$N=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & \\frac{1}{2} & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n| $\\frac{2}{3}M+2N=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $-2$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-12$ | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" 13194139535481 17592186045443 true] [17592186299873 1074 "We multiply each entry of $M$ by $\\frac{2}{3}$ and each entry of $N$ by $2,$ and then add the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}M+2N & =\\frac{2}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 15 \\\\ -12 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & \\frac{1}{2} & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 6 & \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 0 & \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 15 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-12) & \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 6 & \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot 3 & 2\\cdot (-1) & 2\\cdot 0 \\\\ 2\\cdot (-2) & 2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} & 2\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4+6 & 0-2 & 10+0 \\\\ -8-4 & 4+1 & 0-2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & -2 & 10 \\\\ -12 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535481 17592186045443 false] [17592186299873 1074 "We multiply each entry of $M$ by $\\frac{2}{3}$ and each entry of $N$ by $2,$ and then add the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}M+2N & =\\frac{2}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 15 \\\\ -12 & 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+2\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & \\frac{1}{2} & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\